ce my teammate only has 3 cards left versus my 15, and the landlord has 4, I should PASS and give my teammate the chance to play. My teammate is in a much better position to win this game than I am. As a peasant, my goal includes helping my teammate win, not just winning myself.\n\nReason:\nI should pass because my teammate has only 3 cards remaining compared to my 15 cards. In Dou Dizhu, when playing as peasants, we win if EITHER peasant empties their hand before the landlord. My teammate is in a far better position to win (3 cards vs landlord\'s 4) than I am (15 cards vs landlord\'s 4). By passing, I give my teammate the opportunity to play and potentially win the game for our team. Taking control now with 15 cards would be counterproductive when my teammate is so close to victory.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
